# CODEOWNERS
#
# Docs: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# A selective gate, the standard musher-dev/platform set for every repository:
# no `*` catch-all (COMM-09, which no waiver lifts), and owners only on the
# paths whose change alters what this repository enforces or what every
# consumer inherits. To have every change reviewed, raise the ruleset's
# required approvals instead.
# .github/rulesets/main-branch.json pairs `required_approving_review_count: 0`
# with `require_code_owner_review: true`, so a pull request that touches an
# owned path waits for its owner and any other pull request merges on green
# checks. GitHub waives the requirement on the owner's own pull requests.
#
# What is owned, and why:
#   /.github/          the gate itself: this file, the rulesets, the workflows
#                      that run the required checks, the release config
#   /.repo/            the declarations: identity, outputs, and the waivers
#                      that silence this repository's own findings
#   /engineering-conventions/definitions/
#                      the requirements, terms and profiles every consumer
#                      inherits when it pins a release
#   /.claude/hooks/, /.claude/settings.json
#                      the hook and deny rules that stop an agent merging a
#                      pull request or pushing to main
#
# Everything else is unowned on purpose. The checks and tooling are held to the
# definitions by fixtures and CI, and pin, lock and vendored files
# (.config/mise/, .devcontainer/devcontainer-lock.json, checks/data/vendor/,
# checks/schemas/vendor/) stay unowned so bot pull requests merge on green CI.
#
# Syntax rules that bite:
#   - LAST matching pattern wins — order from broad to specific.
#   - ALL owners for a pattern go on ONE line.
#   - Owners need EXPLICIT write access to this repo, or the entry is silently
#     ignored and the path becomes unowned. GitHub lists such lines at
#     `gh api repos/musher-dev/engineering-conventions/codeowners/errors`.
#   - A root-anchored path must exist (COMM-10): after a rename, the old line
#     protects nothing.
#   - Individual @handles until GitHub teams (@musher-dev/<team>) exist.

